  <h2 id="stages">The four stages of a redemption</h2>
  <p>Separate a redemption into these stages when checking a published estimate. A number that covers only processing does not establish the total time from request to receipt.</p>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li><b>Request.</b> You submit the redemption. The operator checks your Sweeps Coins balance, playthrough completion and any daily caps.</li>
    <li><b>Verification (KYC).</b> The operator may check identity, address and payment-method ownership. Check the requirements for the specific operator.</li>
    <li><b>Processing.</b> The operator reviews and releases the payment internally. Check whether a published window starts before or after approval.</li>
    <li><b>Delivery.</b> The payment provider delivers the prize. Check the method's delivery window separately from operator processing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="first-vs-repeat">First redemption vs repeat redemption</h2>
  <p>A first request can include identity checks that a later request may not need. Further checks can still apply to a verified account. Compare first redemptions with first redemptions and repeat requests with repeat requests; do not assume a repeat request has a guaranteed shorter window.</p>

  <h2 id="delays">Why redemptions get delayed</h2>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li class="bad"><b>Identity mismatch.</b> The name or address on your ID does not match the account, or the payment method is in a different name.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Incomplete wagering.</b> Check the playthrough requirement for the specific coin source or promotion. A requirement for purchase-bonus coins may not cover every reward.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Weekend and holiday timing.</b> Bank transfers settle on banking days, so a Friday request can sit until the following week.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Caps and thresholds.</b> Check the current minimum and any limits for the selected redemption method. Do not substitute a gift-card minimum for a cash minimum.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Pending redemption troubleshooting</h2>
  <p>If a redemption sits in a pending state, work through this order before contacting support:</p>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li class="good"><b>Check verification status.</b> If the operator has requested documents, nothing moves until they are approved. Upload clear, current documents that match your account details exactly.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Confirm wagering completion.</b> Check that all Sweeps Coins in the request have met the playthrough requirement.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Check the minimum.</b> Confirm the selected method's threshold in the current redemption screen and applicable rules.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Check the time unit.</b> Confirm whether the operator means business days or calendar days, and when the stated period begins.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Then contact support.</b> Ask for the specific stage your redemption is in: verification, processing or delivery. The answer tells you whether the hold-up is yours to fix or theirs.</li>
  </ul>

